  {
    "sha": "711909722289e4c67e1a3171ab9cbd7f34d46b25",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOKDql7toAKDcxMTkwOTcyMjI4OWU0YzY3ZTFhMzE3MWFiOWNiZDdmMzRkNDZiMjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "MohamedRejeb",
        "email": "mohamedrejeb445@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-07-26T19:39:24Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "MohamedRejeb",
        "email": "mohamedrejeb445@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-07-26T19:39:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(desktop): load native libraries from the system path before JAR extraction\n\nPackagers like Conveyor's extract-native-libraries move native libs out\nof the JARs into the JVM lib dir and rewrite the JARs without them — the\nin-JAR resource lookup then fails and the app crashes (\"Native library\nnot found in JAR resources\"). Try System.loadLibrary first (the same\npattern that keeps Skiko compatible) and fall back to the bundled-\nresource extraction used by dev runs and jpackage builds. Applies to\nboth calf-file-picker and calf-share desktop loaders.",
